error[E0136]: '@jsn' is not an attribute a class accepts
  --> check_json_attr_unknown.bit:13:1
   |
13 | @jsn
   | ^^^^ '@json', '@table', '@timestamps' and '@softDelete' are the class attributes; field attributes go on the fields themselves (SPEC §10.5)
error[E0137]: '@json' takes no arguments
  --> check_json_attr_unknown.bit:18:1
   |
18 | @json("x")
   | ^^^^^^^^^^ write '@json' on its own; per-field key names are set with '@key("...")' on the field
error[E0021]: expected '=', found ':'
  --> check_json_attr_unknown.bit:24:17
   |
24 |   print("${A{ id: 1 }.id}\n")
   |                 ^ class field init uses '=', not ':' -- write 'id = ...' here
